+for byte, so a program can reproduce what the reader is looking at. It is
+therefore a document first and a terminal rendering second: the characters a
+terminal acts on — a right-to-left override, a zero-width mark — are written
+as the value holds them, because a document that differed from the one
+`json.stringify` writes would be a document no program could produce. The
+REPL's `.pretty` and `.table` commands are renderings, and they spell those
+characters out instead.
