## Objective
- Fix all 6 review findings for phase-063 (round 2) in the Redblue crate, without weakening gates, adding `#[ignore]`/`// skip`/`allow(clippy::…)`, or deleting tests; then re-run the four gates.

## Important Details
- Repo/crate root: `/home/runner/work/rbops/rbops/redblue`; harness root: `/home/runner/work/rbops/rbops`.
- The real round-2 findings are in `/home/runner/work/rbops/rbops/logs/phase-063.review.2.log` (user prompt only pasted "FINDINGS: 6"). `review_findings.md` at repo root is a stale phase-062 review — ignore it.
- The 6 findings: (1) `json_stringify` unbounded recursion; (2) `Value::Display` unbounded recursion; (3) `json.stringify` writes `null` for function/builtin/object while `.json` refuses (SPEC drift); (4) `json_escape_text` does not escape terminal-active chars, so `.json` writes them raw; (5) `src/error.rs` `WIDE`/`char_cells` table incomplete (⭐, ✨, ❤️, regional indicators, variation selectors) so caret lands short; (6) `mangles_the_terminal` in `src/repl/render.rs` misses some terminal-active characters.
- Decisions: bound display/JSON depth at `crate::parser::MAX_NESTING_DEPTH` (64); keep `json.stringify` of non-finite numbers as `null`; make `json.stringify` refuse function/builtin/object via catchable `Error::Limit`; escape terminal-active marks with JSON `\uXXXX` (surrogate pairs for astral) in `json_escape_text`, making `.json` and `json.stringify` remain byte-identical; use `unicode-width` (already a transitive dep, confirmed usable) for error caret width.
- Deliberate test modifications (not deletions): `tests/repl_printing_test.rs` `.json` raw-mark test renamed to expect escaping; `tests/stdlib_modules_test.rs::json_unicode_text_survives_stringify_unchanged` split plain unicode vs escaped `\u202b`.
